WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Welcome to a new week on Tesla's short time.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.200
Episode 547, I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.280
Today is July 20th, 2026.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.420
Here's what's kicking off the week in Tesla land.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.100
Tesla's first semi-megacharger station in California

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.520
opens the door to commercial long haul electric trucking

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:20.020
economics.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.660
The station marks the first dedicated public charging

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.140
point for the semi after earlier fleet only deployments.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.620
It supplies the high power needs on commercial routes

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:34.380
and gives early operators the first chance to gather real world

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.880
TCO data on charging times and corridor uptime.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.920
Last covered on July 19th, the semi-program now moves the open

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.500
question of corridor coverage one step forward with visible

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.800
public infrastructure.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.080
Additional sites are expected next to close gaps on long haul

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:52.640
corridors.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:56.480
The same power delivery limits that shape semi-charging

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.360
also apply to stationary storage, where Tesla is now

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.120
expanding reach through partners.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.340
Tesla and ECO soft are collaborating to deploy mega-pack

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:09.400
systems globally through the partner's regional networks.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:13.160
The arrangement targets markets beyond direct utility

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:16.940
contracts and lets local teams handle installation and grid

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:17.580
integration.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.880
It aligns with scaled production at giga Nevada and Texas

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.220
without adding direct sales headcount.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:28.820
Last covered on July 19th, the energy program now gains a

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:31.040
channel for faster geographic coverage.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.820
Initial project announcements will show how the

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:37.240
collaboration converts backlog into installed capacity.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:41.180
While energy scales through partners, the Berlin plant shows

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:44.520
how existing factories can improve margins even before

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.460
volumes recover.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:49.620
The Berlin giga factory posted higher earnings even though

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.040
vehicle output declined.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.820
Improved vehicle mix and cost controls offset the volume drop

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:58.920
and lifted the plant's contribution to overall margins.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.660
The result comes ahead of broader European demand signals

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.680
expected in Q2 results.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:08.420
Observers will watch whether the profit lift holds once

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.820
production volumes recover.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:13.220
The outcome demonstrates that margin gains can

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:16.640
proceed volume recovery when mix and operating discipline

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:17.600
improve first.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.600
The same discipline around scaling timelines appears in

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.500
the humanoid program where visible output is still zero.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.280
No Optimus units have entered production volume ahead of

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:29.960
the earnings call.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.020
Dedicated factory construction at giga Texas continues,

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.300
yet visible output remains at the prototype stage.

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:41.760
Last covered on July 18th, the program still sits at the

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.820
pre-volume phase.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:47.240
The 2027 target stays the next concrete checkpoint.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:51.000
Investors will listen for any updated timeline on when

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.440
hundreds of units per week become feasible.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.180
Power constraints surface again when comparing vehicle

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.280
operating costs.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.960
Real world electricity versus diesel costs for

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:04.420
equivalent monthly mileage show a widespread

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.060
favoring the cyber truck.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:10.240
The comparison uses typical US residential rates and

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.520
fleet diesel prices.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.600
Owners will track whether home solar or time of use plans

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.340
widen the advantage further.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.960
Fleet operators considering the semi will use similar

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:23.560
math once more mega chargers come online.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.300
The data point reinforces the operating cost edge

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.400
already visible in passenger vehicles and now being

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.000
tested at commercial scale.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.900
On the product side, Tesla is marking a different kind of

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.100
milestone at its Los Angeles diner.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.040
The Los Angeles location marks its first

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.260
anniversary on July 21st with Optimus robots,

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.700
roller skating staff, and a limited edition hat

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:48.960
signed by friends.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.460
The event highlights Tesla's continued use of the

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.100
diner as a public showcase for hardware and

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.820
software in a retail setting.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:00.700
Attendance patterns will indicate how well the concept draws

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.520
repeat visitors beyond the initial launch buzz.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.740
The one year mark also tests whether the location can sustain

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.760
foot traffic once novelty fades.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.460
A Chinese EV maker conducted public road autonomous tests

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.680
in central Munich.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.920
The activity shows competitors pushing regulatory

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:22.020
boundaries in Europe while Tesla awaits broader

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:23.700
unsupervised approvals.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.220
Local authorities will decide whether similar testing

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:28.900
permits expand or tighten.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.280
The outcome affects how quickly multiple vendors can

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.580
gather city street data in dense European environments.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:40.560
X-Pang CEO stated the company's upcoming model is close to

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.940
surpassing the model Y in key metrics.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:47.060
The claim positions X-Pang as a direct volume competitor

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:50.660
in the crossover segment where Tesla holds significant share.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:54.580
Pricing and feature details will determine whether the vehicle

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:58.200
reaches buyers before or after any model Y refresh.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.980
Market share shifts in China and Europe will provide

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.540
the first measurable test.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:08.220
A home charger delivers 42 miles of range added per hour

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:10.520
after installation at a new residence.

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:13.880
The faster rate compared with the mobile connector

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.960
reduces overnight charging time for daily driving.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:20.900
This highlights the practical difference between level two wall

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:25.000
connectors and portable cords for households with higher mileage needs.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:29.160
More installs will show how widely owners adopt the upgrade

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:31.680
when moving into homes with dedicated circuits.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:36.420
A Model X completed the full length of the Americas under its own power.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:41.240
The trip demonstrates long distance capability on existing supercharger

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.080
and destination charging networks.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:46.760
It provides real-world data on vehicle reliability

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:50.000
and charging logistics over extreme distances.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:54.340
Future cross-continent records will test whether network density

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:57.240
improvements keep pace with vehicle range gains.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:01.420
Tesla is expanding production in Germany to meet growing demand.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:05.900
Berlin output is increasing this year to address European demand

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.380
and targets higher utilization rates.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:13.580
Profitability gains reported alongside the volume lift suggest the added shifts

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.020
are margin accretive.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:20.120
Delivery trends through the rest of 2026 will confirm whether demand absorbs

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:21.200
the extra vehicles.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:26.980
The profit result on lower prior volume indicates the plant can absorb added output

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:28.900
without immediate margin delusion.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:33.720
Tesla unveiled a $222 pedal less bike for kids.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:38.420
The balanced bike targets young riders with a simple low-cost design.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.060
Availability begins through Tesla's online store and select locations.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:48.820
It extends the brand into early childhood products without overlapping core vehicle lines.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:54.860
Sales volume will reveal whether accessory categories become meaningful incremental revenue.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:07:00.860
The price point positions the item as an accessible entry to the Tesla ecosystem for families.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:05.920
Investor Ross Gerber called out the cabin air filtration feature as essential

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.560
when smoke events increase.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:12.460
Owners in fire-prone regions are testing the modes real-world effectiveness

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:14.500
during poor air quality days.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:19.900
The discussion ties vehicle software features directly to changing climate patterns.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:26.120
Regional usage data during the current fire season will show whether the mode moves from optional

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:33.380
to frequently activated. A $1 paper trick reportedly exposed an autopilot limitation in a controlled

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:39.220
test. The finding highlights edge cases that vision-only setups must still resolve.

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:44.480
Developers will need to close these gaps before unsupervised operation expands.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:49.720
The test adds to the list of documented scenarios that training data must cover

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:56.580
at higher fidelity. Multiple manufacturers including Honda, Tesla and Volkswagen are pulling certain

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:02.620
electric models from the US market. The moves reflect shifting demand patterns and inventory

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:08.940
adjustments. Tesla's participation shows even the segment leader is pruning slower selling variants.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:15.400
The pattern points to a broader reset in which models remain viable as incentives and buyer

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:20.920
preferences evolve. A pompano beach family home was struck by a Tesla overnight.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:27.200
The vehicle caused significant structural damage before occupants fled. Local authorities

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:32.940
are investigating the circumstances. The incident adds to discussions around vehicle security

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:39.680
and post-crash behavior. Police reports will clarify whether the event involved unauthorized use or

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:46.760
a different sequence of events. Alphabet, Tesla and Intel face a combined $6 trillion earnings test.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:52.660
The three companies report within days of each other. Market focus centers on how each balance

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:59.420
is core operations with AI-related investments. Tesla's results will be parsed for any updates on

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:06.320
compute scaling that support both FSD and Optimus Roadmaps. The cluster of reports will give investors

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:11.980
a single window into capital allocation across hardware, software and training infrastructure.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:18.120
There is a challenge worth discussing. Production volume stays at zero despite ongoing factory

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:25.380
construction at Giga, Texas. The gap between prototype work and the 2027 volume target remains the

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:31.100
central open question for the program. Earnings commentary will need to address when hundreds of

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:37.880
units per week become realistic rather than aspirational. Investors tracking the humanoid timeline will

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:43.820
focus on any new detail that narrows the window between current cell output and the first sustained

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:49.820
production run. Charging infrastructure and energy storage share the same underlying constraint.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:56.460
How much power can move through a given connection at any moment sets the limit. A home charger

00:09:56.460 --> 00:10:02.780
adding 42 miles per hour and a mega pack feeding an entire neighborhood. Both run into wire,

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:09.340
transformer and rate limits that no software update can erase. Tesla's decision to open the

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:15.600
first public semi-megacharger therefore tests whether high power DC can scale faster than the grid

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:21.600
upgrades required to support it. The economics of the station will depend on utilization rates that

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:27.380
only appear once multiple fleet customers route through the same corridor on predictable schedules.

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:34.380
The cost comparison between cyber truck charging and F-150 refueling makes the same point in dollars.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:41.720
Electricity at residential rates undercuts diesel on a per mile basis today. Yet that advantage shrinks

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:47.880
once demand charges or limited off-peak windows enter the equation. Fleet operators watching

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:53.020
the new California station will learn whether the infrastructure investment pays for itself through

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:58.460
utilization or whether citing constraints keep the effective cost higher than the headline numbers

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:04.860
suggest. The same arithmetic will apply to any future mega pack deployments that rely on the same

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:11.160
grid connections. Germany's Berlin factory posting higher profits on lower volume shows the same

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:17.680
principle at the manufacturing level. Fixed costs spread across fewer units usually erode margins,

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:23.620
yet mix improvements and operating discipline produce the opposite result. The pattern suggests

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:29.000
that future capacity additions will only lift earnings if they avoid simply replicating the

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:35.340
current cost structure at larger scale. Any expansion that raises average selling price or reduces

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:41.640
variable cost per unit faster than volume grows will preserve the margin lift already visible in the

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:47.940
latest quarter. Keep an eye on the Q2 earnings call for any fresh detail on Optimus Cell production

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:59.980
cadence. And that's a wrap on today's Tesla news. TSLA closed at $380.84 down $10.22, 2.6%.

